    "lab-2026-11-21-yardstick-literature-count": {
      "id": "0ae2qbje1qm5h51mvb3zkxaant",
      "created": "2026-11-21T03:21:22Z",
      "hash": "sha256:330b4405c1a4749c44c4a14b9ce582397dc403d52151b77bcc539bcd9eed079d",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-digital-yardstick-claim",
          "id": "085g7g2r6espw0jasm111s765a",
          "version": 2,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Few alternative-hardware abstracts compare with digital</strong></p>\n<p>Papers on new computing hardware (analog, photonic, thermodynamic, neuromorphic, reservoir, memristor) rarely report, in their abstracts, a result against a named digital baseline. Of 20 abstracts from 2024 on, checked by hand without knowing what an automatic rule had said, one did: 5%. The rule itself flagged 16%, but its hits were passing mentions. We had set 50% in advance as the line for &quot;most papers do&quot;.</p>\n<p>How sure: real data, but abstracts only, one search of 299 articles, and a small hand check. Results tables in the full papers could tell a different story. <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/experiments/e004-yardstick-literature-count/RESULTS.md\">Code and full results</a>.</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
